// The definition of the Forth of the chain (23.15): the text of language 3 that the compiler forth.tw writes, and its words.
// forth_gen.sh turns this file into the tables between the marks "begin generated" and "end generated" of forth.tw.
// A line "=name" starts a template (the text up to the next "=" line); the characters @ ~ % ^ in it are the numbers r1 r2 r3 r4
// (decimal) which the compiler sets before it writes the template. "//" lines are comments. After "=words" every line is
// "word kind routine template" (a "-" is none); a routine is the template of a word of language 3 `:f@ word` which the compiler
// writes at the end once if the word is used; a macro is "word macro number word": the number, then the word.
// A body line that ends with $ loses its line break and the $. "%sys" names the templates which forth.tw uses by name (constants
// t_<name>), "%px" names the words whose number forth.tw uses (px_<name>).
%sys prelude lit lith call callx rcall ret colon fin rthead exhead kz tn1 tn2 tn3 tn4 str1 str2 strch herepush
%px fetch @
%px store !
=prelude
